<title>USA: Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn/Gilead get European Vistide ok.</title>
<headline>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn/Gilead get European Vistide ok.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc and Gilead Sciences Inc said Friday that the Committee for Proprietary Medicinal Products has recommended that Vistide, an intravenous treatment for cytomegalovirus retinitis in patients with AIDS, be cleared for marketing in Europe.</p>
<p>A viral infection of the retina, CMV retinitis is an opportunistic infection that progressively affects a patient's vision over time and may ultimately lead to blindness, a statement from the companies said.</p>
<p>CMV retinitis affects 15 to 40 per cent of AIDS patients, usually those with fewer than 50 CD4 T-cells, the statement said.</p>
</text>
